  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is (AB)⁻¹?', 'B⁻¹A⁻¹.', 9),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How do you find the determinant of a 3×3 matrix?', 'Expand along a row or column using cofactors: a(ei − fh) − b(di − fg) + c(dh − eg).', 10),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What does the determinant of a transformation matrix represent?', 'The area (2D) or volume (3D) scale factor; a negative value means orientation is reversed.', 11),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How can matrices solve simultaneous equations?', 'Write as AX = B, then X = A⁻¹B if A is non-singular.', 12),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What does det A = 0 mean for a system of 3 equations?', 'There is no unique solution: either no solutions (inconsistent) or infinitely many.', 13),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How do three planes with no unique solution appear geometrically?', 'As a sheaf (common line), a prism (no common point), or with parallel planes.', 14),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is det(AB)?', 'det A × det B.', 15),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is the transpose of a matrix?', 'The matrix formed by swapping rows and columns, Aᵀ.', 16),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How do you find the inverse of a 3×3 matrix?', 'Find the matrix of cofactors, transpose it (adjugate), then divide by the determinant.', 17),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is the zero matrix?', 'A matrix in which every element is 0.', 18),
