  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What transformation does (−1 0; 0 1) represent?', 'A reflection in the y-axis.', 20),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What transformation does (0 1; 1 0) represent?', 'A reflection in the line y = x.', 21),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What matrix represents an anticlockwise rotation by θ about the origin?', '(cos θ −sin θ; sin θ cos θ).', 22),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What matrix represents an enlargement by scale factor k about the origin?', '(k 0; 0 k).', 23),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What matrix represents a stretch parallel to the x-axis, scale factor k?', '(k 0; 0 1).', 24),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What does the matrix (1 k; 0 1) represent?', 'A shear with the x-axis invariant: each point moves parallel to the x-axis by k times its y-coordinate.', 25),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How do you find the image of a point under a transformation?', 'Multiply the transformation matrix by the position vector of the point.', 26),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'How do you find the matrix of a transformation?', 'Find the images of the unit vectors i and j (and k); these form the columns.', 27),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is the matrix for a combined transformation "A then B"?', 'BA (the first transformation is on the right).', 28),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is an invariant point?', 'A point that maps to itself under a transformation.', 29),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.2', 'Matrices', 'What is an invariant line?', 'A line where every point on it maps to a point on the same line.', 30),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is a rational function?', 'A function of the form f(x) = p(x)/q(x) where p and q are polynomials.', 1),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How do you find vertical asymptotes of y = p(x)/q(x)?', 'Solve q(x) = 0 (where p(x) ≠ 0).', 2),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How do you find the horizontal asymptote of y = (ax + b)/(cx + d)?', 'y = a/c.', 3),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is the oblique asymptote of y = (x² + 1)/x?', 'y = x, since y = x + 1/x.', 4),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How can you find the range of y = (x² + 1)/(x − 1)?', 'Rearrange into a quadratic in x and use the discriminant ≥ 0 for real x.', 5),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is y = 1/f(x) used for?', 'Sketching the reciprocal graph: roots of f become vertical asymptotes, and maxima become minima.', 6),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How is y = |f(x)| sketched?', 'Reflect the parts of y = f(x) below the x-axis in the x-axis.', 7),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How is y² = f(x) sketched?', 'Plot y = ±√f(x) where f(x) ≥ 0; the graph is symmetric about the x-axis.', 8),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'Solve (x + 1)/(x − 2) > 0.', 'Critical values −1 and 2: x < −1 or x > 2.', 9),
