  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'How do you find stationary points of y = (x² − 3)/(x − 2) without calculus?', 'Rearrange as a quadratic in x with parameter y, and find where the discriminant is zero.', 21),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is a partial fraction decomposition used for in further algebra?', 'Summing series (method of differences) and integration.', 22),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'Sketch key features of y = 1/(x² − 1).', 'Vertical asymptotes at x = ±1, horizontal asymptote y = 0, y-intercept −1, symmetric about the y-axis.', 23),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What does a modulus inequality |x − 3| < 2x require?', 'Consider both cases or square carefully (only valid when both sides are non-negative); solution x > 1.', 24),
  ('Further Mathematics', 'AQA', 'alevel', '1.3', 'Further Algebra & Functions', 'What is the discriminant condition for a line to meet a conic?', 'Substitute to get a quadratic; ≥ 0 means the line meets the curve, = 0 means tangent.', 25),
